# msesh presets — copy to ~/.config/msesh/presets.conf and edit.
#
# One `name = command` per line. These override the built-ins of the same name,
# so redefining `claude` here changes what `msesh build 4 claude` launches.
#
# A preset whose command runs a known agent is detected as an agent pane: it
# can take an effort on the spec — `msesh build myclaude/high` adds that
# agent's own effort flag — and it is what `--lazy` leaves pre-typed rather
# than started. Everything else is run as-is.
#
# A preset that already spells out an effort keeps it; a spec will not add a
# second one.
#
# `msesh preset list` shows what is currently defined, built-ins first;
# `msesh preset edit` opens this file; `msesh help preset` explains the rest.

# --- built-ins, shown here so you can see the shape ---------------------------
# Each is the bare command, with flags left to you.
# shell  = your shell, interactive
# bash   = bash -i          (also: sh)
# pwsh   = powershell.exe -NoLogo   (also: ps)
# cmd    = cmd.exe
# claude = claude
# codex  = codex

# --- your own ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A claude pane that skips the permission prompts:
# yolo = claude --dangerously-skip-permissions

# A claude pane pinned to plan mode:
# plan = claude --permission-mode plan

# A pane that watches a build:
# watch = npm run dev

# A pane for logs:
# logs = tail -f /var/log/whatever.log
